**Date:** 29 October 2026 · **Replaces:** [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).

## Context

The old subject-only rule hid separate causes in #4471. Its prose disagrees with the desk's
computed cause table and interactive duplicate explorer. See the
[signed incident review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) for the evidence and tickets.

## Decision

Read the report and look up its tenant locale, booking form, and channel. Merge only when
the mechanism and affected path establish the same cause. A matching subject or intake tag
does not prove a duplicate. Different subjects can still share a cause. Unknown tenants and
unexplained symptoms stay open for investigation; do not force them into a known bucket.

## Consequences

Triage needs more reading, but engineering receives separate actionable causes. Preserve
unique report IDs and the original evidence. Reconcile counts after each export, and keep
anomalies visible even when the automatic classifier assigns them to an existing cause.
The historical accepted record 0001 remains unchanged.

